                <h3>Vilpa Films Launches Vilpa Talents, a New Initiative to Discover and Develop Emerging
                    Artists</h3>
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2">By Zafira Hafiz</p>

            </div>
            <div class="col s12 m3"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
            <div class="col s12 m8">
                <img class="responsive-img" src="/assets/images/vilpaTalentsNews.jpg" style="border-radius: 25px ;">
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2 center">Vilpa Films Announced the new Initiative to develop Talent in the
                    industry</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col s12 m2"></div>
            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <p>
                    Vilpa Films will be officially launching Vilpa Talents, the company’s talent development program, at
                    the
                    Dubai International Content Market happening from 10th to 11th November, 2026.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The program’s central mission is not only to discover new voices, but to actively develop them. As
                    Alejandro Vilpa, founder of Vilpa Max, shared, “Vilpa Talents is designed to be more than a
                    representation program; it is a long-term commitment to helping artists build sustainable
                    international
                    careers by providing opportunities, mentorship, visibility, and access to productions.”
                </p>
                <p>
                    The program will focus on developing select actors that have previously worked with Vilpa Films, and
                    support their artistic development by granting them top priority for all upcoming film projects.
                    These actors will be chosen for their exceptional creative talent and potential, and will receive
                    direct assistance with shaping their career within the creative vision and standards that define
                    Vilpa Films.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Existing members within the Vilpa Talents pool have also started making their mark. As part of Vilpa
                    Max’s original animated series, Blue Shades, actors Carla Aguilar López and Dimitri Fontaine are set
                    to star as the show’s two central characters, Elisa and Hassan.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Carla Aguilar López previously collaborated with Alejandro Vilpa on his latest short film, The
                    Undertone of David Jansen, where she portrayed the role of Ivana. Dimitri Fontaine, meanwhile, makes
                    his acting debut through the role of Hassan, marking the beginning of his on-screen career.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Together, they represent the type of emerging talent Vilpa Films hopes to identify, support, and
                    develop through the Vilpa Talents initiative, creating opportunities for artists at different stages
                    of their professional journeys.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Vilpa Talents aims to grow its roster over time to include more exclusive talents, who will be
                    promoted internationally through Vilpa Films and Vilpa Max.
                </p>
                <h4 class="bolderFont" style="color: black !important;">
                    About Vilpa Max
                </h4>
                <p>
                    Vilpa Max is a curated streaming platform where award-winning cinema meets bold new voices—featuring
                    Oscar-winning, Oscar-nominated, BAFTA-winning, and Cannes-selected films from around the world. <br>
                    <br>
                    Watch SKIN on Vilpa Max: <br> <br>
                    <a href="https://vilpamax.com/" target="_blank">www.vilpamax.com</a> <br> <br>
                    Available in the UK and across the MENA region.
                </p>

